-PhotoCraft portable mode
+Plervo Photo portable mode
 
-While this file sits next to photocraft.exe, PhotoCraft keeps its preferences, brush presets,
-crash-recovery autosaves and startup state in the PhotoCraftData folder beside it, and writes
-nothing to %APPDATA%. Copy the whole folder to move PhotoCraft with its settings.
+While this file sits next to plervo-photo.exe, Plervo Photo keeps its preferences, brush presets,
+crash-recovery autosaves and startup state in the Plervo PhotoData folder beside it, and writes
+nothing to %APPDATA%. Copy the whole folder to move Plervo Photo with its settings.
 
 Delete this file to use the normal per-user settings folder (%APPDATA%\Photocraft) instead.
-If PhotoCraftData can't be written (for example on a read-only drive), PhotoCraft says so and
+If Plervo PhotoData can't be written (for example on a read-only drive), Plervo Photo says so and
 uses %APPDATA%\Photocraft instead.
